// A path that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error that halts, in both forms
// of mkdir (spec/05-stdlib.md, mkdir): the C library would read the path only
// up to the NUL and name a shorter directory. A consumer that passes the
// String to its host unchanged creates that shorter directory instead.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
print "before";
mkdir("/tmp/loxpp_probe_mkdir_nul" + chr(0) + "tail");
